title: crosswalk
---



```python
crosswalk(source, target, ref=None)
```

Links between two scales: ``geo_id_from``, ``geo_id_to``, ``weight_area``.

## Parameters {.doc-section .doc-section-parameters}

| Name   | Type   | Description                                        | Default    |
|--------|--------|----------------------------------------------------|------------|
| source | str    | The finer scale, e.g. ``"municipality"``           | _required_ |
| target | str    | A coarser scale it nests in, e.g. ``"department"`` | _required_ |

## Returns {.doc-section .doc-section-returns}

| Name   | Type             | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                          |
|--------|------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|        | pandas.DataFrame | ``weight_area`` is the share of the source unit's area inside the target unit (1.0 for nested scales). Crosswalks are published for every pair of active scales where one nests in the other, from finer to coarser. |

## Example {.doc-section .doc-section-example}

```python
!pip install -q geo4bolivia
import geo4bolivia as geo
import plotly.express as px

xw = geo.crosswalk("municipality", "department")
n = xw.groupby("geo_id_to", as_index=False).size()
n["department"] = n["geo_id_to"].map(geo.units("department")
                                     .set_index("geo_id")["name"])
px.bar(n, x="department", y="size", title="Municipalities per department")
```


